{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3FVmVACoDHmNvbBvbCF","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything. Adding the daily breakdown to `out/summary.csv` would break the file's limits, and the partner would get bad data without any error.\n\nPer the README, the partner portal only accepts `period,total,count` and silently cuts off anything past 50 lines. The file now has 12 monthly rows plus the header. A daily breakdown for 2025 adds up to 365 rows, so the portal would quietly drop most of the year. The partner wouldn't see an error, just missing data.\n\nSome options:\n1. **Separate file:** add the daily breakdown as, say, `out/summary_daily.csv` and leave `summary.csv` as it is. This only works if the partner can pull a second file, which I can't check from here.\n2. **Coarser periods:** weekly rows (about 53) still go over the limit, so that doesn't work either.\n3. **Change the portal's limit:** that's on the partner's side.\n\nCan you check with the partner whether option 1 works for them, or whether they had something else in mind? Once I know, I'll build it from `scripts/summarize.py` and commit.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens":18971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":506,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-32>","timestamp":"2026-11-14T17:55:42.014Z","request_id":"gen-1794678937-C3Rq17mK56ypJuo7qg34"}
